{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 pre-repair review defect RCA (2026-08-14)\\n\\nProblem: the new clone_topology_template helper remints .env-id and legacy .signing-key but leaves asymmetric .opcert-key/.opcert-key.pub copied verbatim.\\n\\nConfirmed mechanism: tests/_topology_template.py:_IDENTITY_FILES and _remint_store_identities enumerate only .env-id and .signing-key. A runtime experiment initialized a real rebar store, generated its op-cert key through rebar.signing.ensure_opcert_key, cloned it twice through clone_topology_template, and compared SHA-256 digests without exposing key material. Template, clone A, and clone B all had the same private-key digest (77e03e4b35385449) and identical public-key bytes, while opcert_principal reported three distinct environment principals. This confirms that clones with distinct environment identity authenticate using one copied private key; the alternative that op-cert material was regenerated or omitted was rejected.\\n\\nDefect legitimacy: this violates the ticket acceptance criterion that per-test copies cannot share environment IDs or signing keys and the helper's own contract that every rebar identity is reminted. The authoritative asymmetric key location and first-use generation contract are src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:28-30 and ensure_opcert_key at lines 152-186.\\n\\nCaller-dependency sweep: the expected behavior is that copying a keyed template never copies private signing authority. clone_topology_template is used only by test fixture builders; no consumer relies on shared key bytes, and current optimized templates generally remain keyless. The safe behavior is to discard copied .opcert-key plus derivative .pub from each copied tracker, preserving lazy first-use generation. No behavioral dependency blocks repair."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786755718022419001,"uuid":"2baf7055-c81a-4f43-8297-33a875d721a1"}